rows=[('02:35–03:11','Survey Consent & Enumeration','Sponsor choices; informed consent; respondent; labelled sample enumerators; community; serial number; address; device GPS, accuracy and capture time; Nigeria State/FCT → LGA → ward.'),('03:21–03:37','Headship & Household Composition','Household name and head; total household heads; complete-list confirmation. Existing roster fields retained.'),('03:37–04:29','Household Member Details','Repeatable member editor: names, relationship, sex, age/DOB, marital status; phone; NIN/tracking number and matching confirmation; NIMC names; account/BVN; work activity, education, school, healthcare, disability, chronic illness and social group. NIN authentication remains unconnected, as stated in the meeting.'),('04:29–04:54','Living & Dwelling Characteristics','Roof, wall, flooring, tenure, room count, drinking water, sanitation, lighting and cooking-fuel choices use native reference values.'),('04:54–05:00; 13:46–13:55','Income, Shocks & Coping','Income-source choices, optional monthly income, shock question and conditional multiple shock choices.'),('05:00–05:11; 13:46–13:55','Health Insurance Coverage','Household insurance Yes/No choice.'),('05:11–05:20','Assets & Possessions','Ownership choices for the 18 demonstrated asset categories; conditional television/generator counts. Existing detailed asset records remain available.'),('05:20–05:44','Crops & Confirmation','Conditional multiple crop selection; explicit accuracy/eligibility acknowledgement before review; native save/submit confirmation.')]
trs=''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(c)+'</td>' for c in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)
checkshtml=''.join('<li>'+html.escape(t)+'</li>' for t in ['Eight-section browser walkthrough: save, resume, member editing and conditional fields passed; zero page JavaScript errors.','Repeated saves preserve the same household/member UUIDs, their link, and all survey values.','Two independent approvals publish the enriched household and member fields. The final check also verifies submitted coordinates, accuracy, device time and selected ward in the master record.','Server rejects missing confirmation/members, malformed NIN/account numbers, mismatched ID confirmation, missing owned-asset counts and incomplete conditional crop/shock answers.','Five native registry accounts passed login/permission checks. Both service home pages still pass their consolidated-card and wording checks.','Collect version 2026111304 passes ODK Validate. Mapping preserves the expanded fields, GPS metadata and state/LGA/ward hierarchy, and rejects an invalid child/parent combination. Previous form versions are retained.','Historical reconciliation passed: 615 native-row comparisons and 391 original AWE rows unchanged. Original master totals remain 90 households and 219 individuals. Approval/validation fixtures removed; the labelled sample draft remains.'])
page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Master Registry household workflow verification</title><style>body{{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;color:#173e34;background:#f0f5ef;margin:0}}main{{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px}}h1,h2{{color:#155e4f}}section{{background:white;border:1px solid #ccdbd0;padding:24px;border-radius:16px;margin:22px 0}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}}th,td{{padding:14px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce7df;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}}a{{color:#12644f}}img{{max-width:100%;border:1px solid #d0ded4;border-radius:12px}}.pass{{font-weight:700;color:#146534}}@media(max-width:650px){{main{{padding:16px}}table,tbody,tr,td,th{{display:block}}}}</style><main><h1>Household workflow: native Master Registry</h1><p>13 November 2026 · Meeting reference: <strong>27_meeting_edited.mp4</strong> and the supplied meeting memo. Implemented directly in the existing registry using its green, responsive design.</p><section><p class="pass">Verified and deployed</p><p><a href="https://g2p-register.wverve.in/en">Open Master Registry</a> · <a href="https://g2p-register.wverve.in/en/intake-form/household/submission/94873215-4e15-489c-b656-e30250c26b03">Open the retained sample draft</a> (authorised officer account).</p><p>The sample household/member and enumerator choices are explicitly fictional. Automated test records used for approvals were removed. No standalone MBR workflow was introduced.</p></section><section><h2>Meeting-to-form comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Video reference</th><th>Native section</th><th>Implemented fields and behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody>{trs}</tbody></table></section><section><h2>Verification evidence</h2><ul>{checkshtml}</ul><p><a href="verification/survey-ui.json">Browser checks</a> · <a href="verification/survey-draft-identity.json">Draft identity</a> · <a href="verification/household-parity-location-test.json">Final approval and GPS</a> · <a href="verification/survey-offline-mapping.json">Offline mapping</a> · <a href="verification/preservation.json">Historical reconciliation</a> · <a href="verification-report.html">Earlier meeting-wide workflow verification</a></p></section><section><h2>Android device acceptance passed</h2><p>A physical Android 16 phone captured real GPS offline, reopened its draft, finalised in airplane mode and automatically synced after reconnecting. The scheduled worker created native intake with normal pending approvals and preserved member, ward and GPS data. The follow-up device check verified stable capture time and submission ID in version 2026111304. See the <a href="../android-flow-verification/verification.html">physical Android verification report</a>. National ID authentication remains future scope. The memo’s bulk-import approval bypass and future programme/payment modules were not enabled by this household-form change.</p></section><section><h2>Native form previews</h2><p><a href="verification/survey-native-location.png">Consent, Nigeria location selectors and GPS</a> · <a href="verification/survey-native-mobile.png">Mobile layout</a></p><img src="verification/survey-member-dialog.png" alt="Native member editor with the registry design"></section><section><h2>Reference provenance</h2><p>The location catalogue matches the existing mobile snapshot: 37 states/FCT, 774 LGAs, 8,799 wards. Existing native state/LGA IDs are preserved through a name-based crosswalk with one explicit Nasarawa/Nassarawa spelling alias in Kano. Source: <a href="https://github.com/open-admin-data/nigeria-administrative-divisions">Open Admin Data, Nigeria administrative divisions</a>, CC BY 4.0, snapshot 4 November 2026.</p><p>The Collect release uses the official <a href="https://docs.getodk.org/central-api-form-management/">ODK versioned draft/publish API</a> and retains previous form definitions.</p></section></main></html>'''
(ROOT/'household-workflow-verification.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8');print('Built household-workflow-verification.html')
